[200.99518, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[3;29r\u001b[29;1H\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;30r\u001b[14;120H┃\r\u001b[5B────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\r\n \u001b[1mCopilot needs information.\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n How should legacy mobile apps handle mandatory refund reasons? I recommend enforcing reasons at activation and\r\n directing affected users to the updated web form, because it meets R2 without inventing reasons.\u001b[K\r\n\r\n \u001b[1mLegacy mobile reason collection:\r\n\u001b[C\u001b[36m❯ Enforce reasons at activation; notify users in advance and direct legacy apps to the updated web form.\r\n\u001b[3C\u001b[mStage mobile updates before enforcing reasons; accept that R2 activation may be delayed.\r\n   Other (type your answer)\r\n\r\n \u001b[1m↑/↓\u001b[m select · \u001b[1menter\u001b[m accept · \u001b[1mctrl+d\u001b[m d"]
